Technical Details

Initial access: Valid credentials
Credential source: Infostealer logs
Reported malware: RedLine, Lumma, Vidar
Platforms: ShareFile, ownCloud, Nextcloud
MFA: Reportedly absent on affected accounts
Known CVE: None established as necessary for the documented campaign
Zero-day exploitation: Not established
Credential reuse / longevity: Reported as material in some cases
Data theft: Reported across multiple organizations
Threat actor: Zestix / Sentap

ownCloud specifically said the relevant attacks did not involve a zero-day or platform vulnerability; stolen credentials were used to sign into accounts that lacked MFA.

Why This Matters

This campaign demonstrates that an organization can run a fully patched cloud file-sharing platform and still lose large quantities of sensitive data if identity controls remain weak.

The attack path effectively bypassed the vulnerability-management problem entirely.

The attacker did not need:

Remote code execution
A zero-day
A web shell
Privilege escalation
A sophisticated exploit chain

The attacker needed:

a valid username and password that still worked.

